{
  "doc": "The content-block chain, shared by server/specs/ContentBlockChain.tla and the Rust test `content_block_chain_instances` (server/crates/domain/src/rules/content_chain_instances_tests.rs). `blocks` are abstract blocks with the JSON each is realised as: `kind` is its `type`, `members` its other members, and `inner` names the block an unwrap reaches through its `inner` member. A `foreign` block is a value no declared case recognises, normalised only by the engine's own steps: `canonical` (already a SideML block, passed through), `fallback` (the media and unknown fallbacks answer it) or neither. Each instance declares cases at the four positions; a `text` case reads one member and builds only from a string, an `unwrap` case normalises its `inner` member in the block's place. The model checks the whole chain over every block of every instance; the Rust test checks each position of the engine against the model's answer for that position, and the foreign blocks against the engine's whole chain. `refused` instances must be refused by the compiler, and `expect` lists hand-written answers - the case that answers a block as a message's content and as a returned value, `canonical`, `fallback` or `none` - that the model and the engine must both give.",
